---
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Doc
  title="About this site"
  summary="What this is, who maintains it, and how to contribute."
  kicker="About"
  sidebar={false}
  wide={true}
  image="/og/about.png"
>
  <p>
    <strong>{site.name}</strong> is the home of <em>AI Governance Engineering: A Manifesto &amp; Body
    of Knowledge</em> — a founding text and working reference for turning AI governance obligations
    into policy-as-code, eval gates, agent registries and machine-readable evidence. It treats
    governance as a system to be built, run and measured, not a document to be signed.
  </p>

  <h2>Who maintains it</h2>
  <p>
    Written and maintained by {site.author}, AI Governance Engineer. Author of the Manifesto &amp;
    Body of Knowledge v{site.bokVersion}. The text is written to be co-authored: it is a first public
    draft, deliberately incomplete, and it invites practitioners who build governance for AI systems
    to sharpen it.
  </p>

  <h2>How to contribute</h2>
  <p>
    Everything here lives in a public repository. Propose a change, add a pattern, sharpen an
    argument or fix a fact by opening a pull request — every factual claim needs a sourced, verified
    citation, following the style guide. Co-authors and contributors are credited by name.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/about/contributors">Contributors and signatories</a> — who has written, revised or
      signed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/about/changelog">Changelog</a> — what changed in each version.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${site.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source repository on
      GitHub</a> — open an issue or a pull request.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Licence</h2>
  <p>
    This work is licensed under <strong>{site.license}</strong>. It may be freely copied and shared
    with attribution to {site.author} and contributors.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Discuss the discipline on{' '}
    <a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>, or on{' '}
    <a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>
